In article <1992Apr14.201125.11289@unlinfo.unl.edu>, ksoutor@unlinfo.unl.edu (kevin soutor) writes:
> I am having a problem saving my Nethack character.  I am 
> running the game on a 640K Generic PC.  The game will 
> indicate that the character has been saved but on the 
> subsequent boot off of the hard drive the program refuses to
> recognize my character's name.  Then Nethack starts 
> normally, preceeded by the cryptic runes "Saved game out of 
> date".  Has anyone had a similar problem?  What is the fix? 

This sounds like you don't set your clock.  Remember, if you play for two
hours, the time is noe 2 am (If you don't set your clock) on 1-1-80.  If you
save then reboot the computer, The time is 12am 1-1-80 and the game is rightly
confused about how the HELL you're continuing a game that DOESN'T (shouldn't)
exsist yet.  So, set your clock correctly every time before playing. :)

